            "revisions"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Uneven gains",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Food services and drinking places added 59,000 jobs; local government education added 42,000. Local government education largely reversed July’s fall and has changed little overall since January 2025. Information employment fell 23,000. That mix cautions against treating August’s improvement as broad-based.",
          "kind": "analysis",
          "claim_ids": [
            "mix"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Average hourly earnings rose 0.3% in August and 3.1% over the year. Those figures measure wages, not consumer inflation.",
          "kind": "fact",
          "claim_ids": [
            "wages"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "What remains open for the Fed",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "On July 29, 2026, the Fed held its target range at 3.5%-3.75% by a 9-3 vote. All three dissenters preferred a quarter-point increase. Its statement described solid economic expansion and inflation above its 2% goal, partly reflecting supply shocks including energy.",
          "kind": "fact",
          "claim_ids": [
            "july_policy",
            "fed_inflation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For readers assessing interest-rate policy, stronger hiring provides employment evidence but does not resolve the Fed’s inflation concerns or establish its next action.",
